{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Approximation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Approximation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the maximum number of balls of clay of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that can completely fit inside a cube of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> assuming the balls can be reshaped but not compressed before they are packed in the cube?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155828867f43df017eeb34cfaacde7f881e7d8b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }4\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }5\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Inequality)\">Solution 1 (Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/8/f88d205b2a8e2a1387cf23c46211012e3dc6f609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_{\\text{cube}}=6^3=216,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /> and the volume of a clay ball is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d63a409df32674736ac9f40f22894d4cb0cef61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_{\\text{ball}}=\\frac43\\cdot\\pi\\cdot2^3=\\frac{32}{3}\\pi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"188\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since the balls can be reshaped but not compressed, the maximum number of balls that can completely fit inside a cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f83af535939f012c6656b2092471491bfc74031.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\lfloor\\frac{V_{\\text{cube}}}{V_{\\text{ball}}}\\right\\rfloor=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"43\" />\nApproximating with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa900d92b8dfe46c8910fd74fa94af405b052a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\approx3.14,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11fb20842d6dd84a7ac0e8844161854afd76fed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12&lt;4\\pi&lt;13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/33066043335762ca42484a106b6f8869a216b3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{13}\\right\\rfloor \\leq \\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor \\leq \\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{12}\\right\\rfloor.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"189\" height=\"45\" /> We simplify to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f45161187af5380eb38c83ca2df2390d0f2467.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6 \\leq \\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor \\leq 6,\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"43\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf5fabe53a9c4b657c20a09b51a39756ea63e9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"132\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~NH14 ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Inequality)\">Solution 2 (Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown in Solution 1, we conclude that the maximum number of balls that can completely fit inside a cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4312cce56ade78734dd043b21390fdf3e82ba7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"55\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>By an underestimation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea1bda14b351e4e80c04b10498bffa2af6512b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\approx3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8607bce5140470ddaefbdf3aacc013a8099010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi&gt;12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae4ca17ae917f644c053b808104e916b50aec1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81}{4\\pi}&lt;6\\frac34.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By an overestimation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca85e4da35442dceed6281e569c1b6085f353fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\approx\\frac{22}{7},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8521b43912f85b295f87441be4eb3678ba1103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi&lt;\\frac{88}{7},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/51882fabedccb7e3fc98d647ba2a8b784ceba173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81}{4\\pi}&gt;6\\frac{39}{88}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Together, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723449faf3bdc4facff3f2a7e2730fe65e46d5f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6 &lt; 6\\frac{39}{88} &lt; \\frac{81}{4\\pi} &lt; 6\\frac34 &lt; 7,\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf5fabe53a9c4b657c20a09b51a39756ea63e9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"132\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Approximation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Approximation)\">Solution 3 (Approximation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Approximation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown in Solution 1, we conclude that the maximum number of balls that can completely fit inside a cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4312cce56ade78734dd043b21390fdf3e82ba7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"55\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Approximating with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea1bda14b351e4e80c04b10498bffa2af6512b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\approx3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0ae03c0e4589ba5d27679e940dadf745cc78fc1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\approx6\\frac34.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbf33b81900fa9e836a608be7484b4c4d6ea3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> it is safe to claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf5fabe53a9c4b657c20a09b51a39756ea63e9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{81}{4\\pi}\\right\\rfloor=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"132\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0WrcZI_z9IE\">https://youtu.be/0WrcZI_z9IE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qOiO45IsE54\">https://youtu.be/qOiO45IsE54</a>\n</p><p>~Charles3829\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/o98vGHAUYjM?t=158\">https://youtu.be/o98vGHAUYjM?t=158</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VcGR0GVqKBI\">https://youtu.be/VcGR0GVqKBI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A\">2021 Fall AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017031823\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 248/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2470/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 304/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5540/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.136      1 -total\n 59.35%    8.390      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.71%    5.613      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22181:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017031823 and revision id 199867. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}